  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="27f89513-b766-5bcc-b074-6440e7b399e1" activityNameId="a9d4c2b7-95b8-5816-aa38-4d0015b9ffaa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant
The material and energy requirements for construction have been roughly estimated on the basis of the data from an old US reference and scaling them down by the ratio of the capacities (centrifuge process is modular, therefore in first approximation linearity can be assumed for requirements). It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning. Transport requirements recalculated either using ecoinvent standard distances for Europe (e.g. for chemicals) or given average distances by train from Chinese 2004 statistics or own assumptions. This dataset has been developed with the goal to serve a preliminary estimation of the Chinese nuclear chain for the Chinese electricity mix. Hence, it cannot be used for comparisons of centrifuge enrichment infrastrucure among countries.;
UUID: 37c060d3-7997-3b82-8484-cc4231514484
The module includes: estimated land use of a plant with capacity of 1500 t SWU (separative work unit); energy (electricity, diesel, and light oil) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Available construction material and energy data refer to a model plant in early 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_37c060d3-7997-3b82-8484-cc4231514484.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
